From 8af6c4c55854dff79ab0db68d7170fad0e083571 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Angel Martinez <110217098+anmartinez1256@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 08:46:30 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 49/49] Dispersive operator setup on the setup threads, setup
 memory back to the OS

Building the Lorentz / Drude and Debye operator extensions walked the
whole grid on one thread and asked the material lookup for a
dynamic_cast per cell; at 30 M cells with half the cells dispersive the
setup took 13 s where the rest of the operator takes 2 s, and the
freed setup arrays stayed in the process (5.9 GiB resident).

The two BuildExtension scans now run per x-line on the operator's setup
pool: each thread collects its lines' entries in blocks, the blocks are
merged in x order, which is the serial order, so every array is the
same byte for byte at any pool size. Columns that hold no wanted,
unmarked primitive are skipped. Operator::GetMaterial remembers the
cast per thread and setup generation. The EC arrays and the scan blocks
come from SetupAlloc / SetupFree (tools/setup_memory.h: mmap on macOS,
malloc elsewhere), so freed setup memory leaves the process. The
engine's SetupLines skips its stable sort when the positions are
already sorted by x and tests first-component uniqueness with a bitmap.

OPENEMS_SETUP_THREADS=n sets the pool size; OPENEMS_SETUP_TIMING=1
prints the new phases (tools/setup_timing.h). No per-timestep function
changes.

Checked bit-identical against the commit before and against v0.37.0:
operator arrays by hash at pool sizes 1, 2, 3, 6 and default on 22
models, 470 box configurations, the dispersive check at 50 k and 1 M
cells and on the closed cylinder, five models without dispersion, the
Debye check, six models at three thread settings and the validation
suite; six of eight planted faults caught (the two others need an
index pattern no test model has).

Mac Studio (M5 Max), upstream bench.py with a source, 18 threads,
before -> after: dispersive case at 30 M cells setup 13.25 -> 4.90 s,
resident memory 5857 -> 3737 MiB; at 8 M cells 3.63 -> 1.55 s, 1742 ->
1069 MiB; antenna case at 30 M 4.09 -> 2.87 s, 4600 -> 3872 MiB; PML
case 3872 -> 3154 MiB. Rates 0.98 to 1.01 of before on ten points.

